schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Donating appreciated crypto directly can avoid US donor capital gains tax"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    For US donors, donating appreciated crypto directly (rather than selling
    then donating cash) can mean no capital gains tax owed, and donors can
    deduct the full fair market value; for the receiving organization,
    charitable donations generally are not subject to income tax.
  evidence: >-
    Attributed in-article to "CryptoAltruists" as the source.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/compliance-legal.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used to explain why crypto donations can be more tax-advantageous than
    cash for a donor, and reassure orgs about their own tax exposure.
  uncertainty: >-
    Same single secondary source as the property-treatment claim; jurisdiction-
    and individual-situation-specific in practice — not verified against a
    primary IRS source here.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: not-public-yet
  high_risk: true
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/compliance-legal.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-f8cf63c4e847
